 *
 * Every collaborator used by the domain / selectors / services is resolved through
 * the factories declared here, so that tests can swap in fflib mocks by calling
 * `setMock(...)` on the relevant factory (UnitOfWork, Service, Selector, Domain).
 *
 * Note: Apex initialises static fields in declaration order, therefore the
 * `Selector` factory is declared before the `Domain` factory and can safely be
 * handed over to it. That guarantees that building a domain from a set of record
 * ids queries the records through the very same (mockable) selector factory.
 */
public inherited sharing class Application {

    /**
     * Unit of work factory.
     *
     * Registers Account, Contact, Opportunity and OpportunityContactRole so that a
     * single commit is able to insert new Accounts, Contacts, Opportunities that
     * belong to those new Accounts, and the OpportunityContactRoles that link the
     * new Opportunities to the new Contacts - with all of the relationships
     * registered through the unit of work.
     *
     * The foreign key / relationship fields are part of the field lists so that
     * `registerRelationship(...)` and `registerNew(...)` can resolve and populate
     * them correctly on commit.
     */
    public static fflib_Application.UnitOfWorkFactory UnitOfWork =
        new fflib_Application.UnitOfWorkFactory(
            new Map<Schema.SObjectType, List<Schema.SObjectField>>{
                Account.SObjectType => new List<Schema.SObjectField>{
                    Account.Id,
                    Account.Name,
                    Account.Rating,
                    Account.Industry,
